/-!
# Local types of modules under the comparison functor of a topology

Descent, Lemma 05VG compares fifteen properties of modules — the seven global ones of Modules
on Sites, Definition 03DE, the eight local ones of Definitions 03DL and 03ER — across the
equivalences `QCoh(𝒪_S) ⟶ QCoh((Sch/S)_τ, 𝒪)` and `QCoh(𝒪_S) ⟶ QCoh(S_τ, 𝒪)`, `𝓕 ↦ 𝓕ᵃ`, of
Descent, Proposition 03DX, for `τ` any of the Zariski, étale, smooth, syntomic and fppf
topologies.  The source excepts "locally free" and "coherent" from the claim, and reinstates
"coherent" only for the small site, only for `τ` Zariski or étale, and only over a locally
Noetherian base.

`StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.GlobalTypesUnderComparison` proves the seven
**global** clauses.  **This file is the second half, and it covers four of the eight local
clauses**: local generation by `r` sections (03DL (4)), being of finite type (03DL (5)), finite
presentation (03DL (7)) and flatness (03ER (3)).

## Which comparison is carried, and why it is not the one the first half carries

The global clauses say that a module is built out of the structure sheaf by coproducts and
cokernels, so the first half could carry 03DX as a mere functor `Φ` between the two categories
of sheaves of modules, asking only that it be full, faithful, coproduct-preserving and
unit-preserving.  A local clause is not a condition on the module alone: it quantifies over the
objects of the site and over coverings of them, and a functor between categories of modules
cannot see either.  So the comparison has to be carried at the level at which coverings exist.

It is carried here as **a morphism of ringed topoi `f : X ⟶ Y` whose pushforward is an
equivalence and whose structure map is invertible**, with `𝓕 ↦ 𝓕ᵃ` taken to be
`Stacks.Sheaves.RingedToposModules.RingedToposHom.pullbackModules f`. Three consequences of that
choice are
worth stating plainly.

* It is **stronger than 03DX**.  03DX gives an equivalence of the categories of quasi-coherent
  modules; it does not give an equivalence of the ringed topoi.  The one case of 05VG in which
  the comparison morphism of ringed topoi *is* an equivalence is the small Zariski site, whose
  topos of sheaves is the topos of sheaves on the scheme.  It is not an equivalence for the
  small étale site, nor for a big site at any of the five `τ`, so for those cases the
  hypothesis carried here is strictly stronger than what 03DX supplies.
* It is **not vacuous**, and it is the only level at which the library can state these clauses
  at all: the four results below are Modules on Sites, Lemma 03DM (and, for flatness, its
  analogue) applied to that morphism, and 03DM is a statement about equivalences of ringed
  topoi.
* The **forward implication alone** — `𝓕` has `𝒫` implies `𝓕ᵃ` has `𝒫` — needs no equivalence:
  it is Modules on Sites, Lemma 03DO for the three clauses of 03DL and Lemma 05VD for
  flatness, each stated in this library for an arbitrary morphism of ringed topoi, hence valid
  for all five `τ` and for the big and the small site alike.  Those are
  `Stacks.Sheaves.LocalGeneration.pullbackModules_isLocallyGeneratedByOnSite`,
  `Stacks.Sheaves.FiniteType.pullbackModules_isFiniteType`,
  `Stacks.Sheaves.FinitePresentation.isFinitePresentation_pullbackModules` and
  `Stacks.Sheaves.RingedToposModules.isFlat_pullbackModules`.  No 05VG tag is carried by them:
  05VG asserts an equivalence, and half of an equivalence does not realize the clause.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Sheaves.LocalTypeComparison.isFlat_iff`: **Descent, Lemma 05VG for Modules on Sites,
  Definition 03ER (3)**, flatness.  A quasi-coherent module is flat if and only if its image
  under the comparison is.  This is the one clause here that the library did not already have
  in equivalence form, so it is proved rather than registered.
* The clauses 03DL (4), (5) and (7) are registered against the three statements of Modules on
  Sites, Lemma 03DM already in the library, by the `add_to_stacks` commands at the end of this
  file.  Restating them here would only duplicate them: once 03DX is carried as an equivalence
  of ringed topoi, 05VG for a local clause *is* 03DM for that clause.

## The four clauses not covered

* **Locally free** (03DL (1)) is left open here, and that is faithful rather than a shortfall:
  05VG itself excepts it.
* **Finite locally free** (03DL (2)) and **locally generated by sections** (03DL (3)) are
  claimed by 05VG but are not reachable at this level of generality: the library has no 03DO
  for them, and the step they need is the localization over an object of the comparison, Modules
  on Sites, Section 03DG.  That localization *is* available when the comparison is presented by
  a special cocontinuous functor of sites — it is
  `Stacks.LocalizedDenseSubsite.sliceEquivalence`, and the three clauses are then Modules on
  Sites, Lemma 03DM, proved in
  `StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.LocalTypesUnderSpecialCocontinuous` — but the
  comparison of Descent, Proposition 03DX is not of that shape, so those statements do not
  apply to it.  Localizing a morphism of ringed topoi that is *not* presented by a functor of
  sites is still not constructed in the tree, which is also what stops quasi-coherence,
  03DL (6), from being transported here.
* **Coherent** (03DL (8)) is not treated *here*.  05VG's claim for it is restricted to
  `QCoh(𝒪_S) ⟶ QCoh(S_τ, 𝒪)` with `S` locally Noetherian and `τ` Zariski or étale, and the
  source's argument is to replace coherence by finite type over a locally Noetherian scheme
  using Cohomology of Schemes, Lemma 01XZ.  That reduction is a statement about *schemes*: it
  needs `S` and its Noetherian hypothesis, and the small `τ`-site of `S`, none of which appear
  in a statement about an abstract morphism of ringed topoi.  Stating it at this level of
  generality would either drop the restriction, which would make the statement false, or carry
  a scheme-level hypothesis that the ringed-topos comparison cannot use.  The pieces the
  eventual proof needs are in the library: 01XZ as
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherenceCriteria.coherent_tfae`, coherence on a site as
  `SheafOfModules.IsCoherentOnSite`, and — as for the clauses (2), (3) and (6) above — its
  transport along a comparison presented by a special cocontinuous functor of sites, which is
  03DM for the clause and is
  `Stacks.Sheaves.SpecialCocontinuous.isCoherentOnSite_iff`.  What is missing for 05VG is again
  only that the comparison of 03DX is not of that shape.

