-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry
open Stacks.Sheaves.RingedToposModules

namespace Stacks.Sheaves.LocalTypeComparison

universe u

variable {X Y : RingedTopos.{u, u, u}}
  [X.J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u})]
  [Y.J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u})]
  [X.J.HasSheafCompose (forget RingCat.{u})]
  [Y.J.HasSheafCompose (forget RingCat.{u})]
  [X.J.HasSheafCompose (forget AddCommGrpCat.{u})]
  [Y.J.HasSheafCompose (forget AddCommGrpCat.{u})]
  [HasWeakSheafify X.J AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [HasWeakSheafify Y.J AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [X.J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [Y.J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]

/-- **Descent, Lemma 05VG for Modules on Sites, Definition 03ER (3): flatness.**  A sheaf of
modules on the target of an equivalence of ringed topoi is flat if and only if its image under
the comparison is flat.

The forward implication is Modules on Sites, Lemma 05VD,
`Stacks.Sheaves.RingedToposModules.isFlat_pullbackModules`, which holds for an arbitrary
morphism of ringed topoi.  The reverse one applies 05VD to the inverse morphism
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.inverse` and carries the conclusion back along
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.pullbackModulesInverseObjIso`, the identification of the
round trip with the identity, using that flatness is invariant under isomorphism of sheaves of
modules.  This is the pattern of the three statements of Modules on Sites, Lemma 03DM in
`StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.ModuleTypesUnderEquivalence`, which flatness is
not a clause of, 03DM covering 03DL rather than 03ER.

The three universes of each ringed topos are taken equal because
`Stacks.Sheaves.RingedToposModules.isFlat_pullbackModules` already forces the source's object
and section universes to agree; applying it to `f` and to the inverse of `f` in turn forces the
same of the target, and the round-trip isomorphism needs the two section universes to agree. -/
@[stacks 05VG "flat; local properties, with the comparison of 03DX carried as an equivalence \
of ringed topoi rather than of quasi-coherent modules alone", sga "4 V 1.7.1" "special case"]
theorem isFlat_iff (f : AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom X Y)
    [f.toToposHom.pushforward.IsEquivalence] [IsIso f.fSharp]
    (F : SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (J := Y.J)) Y.O)) :
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsFlat (O := Y.O) F ↔
      Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsFlat (O := X.O)
        ((f.toModulesHom.pullbackModules).obj F) := by
  refine ⟨fun hF ↦ ?_, fun hP ↦ ?_⟩
  · exact isFlat_pullbackModules f.toModulesHom F hF
  · exact Stacks.ModuleUp.isFlat_of_iso (O := Y.O)
      (AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.pullbackModulesInverseObjIso f F)
      (isFlat_pullbackModules (AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.inverse f).toModulesHom _ hP)

end Stacks.Sheaves.LocalTypeComparison

/-! ## The three clauses of 03DL that Modules on Sites, Lemma 03DM already states

Each of the following three declarations says exactly that the clause of Modules on Sites,
Definition 03DL holds for a module on the target of an equivalence of ringed topoi if and only
if it holds for its pullback.  With Descent, Proposition 03DX carried as such an equivalence,
that is Descent, Lemma 05VG for the clause, so the tag is registered against the existing
declaration rather than duplicated onto a restatement of it. -/

add_to_stacks 05VG "locally generated by r sections; local properties, with the comparison of \
03DX carried as an equivalence of ringed topoi rather than of quasi-coherent modules alone"
  AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.isLocallyGeneratedByOnSite_iff_pullbackModules

add_to_stacks 05VG "finite type; local properties, with the comparison of 03DX carried as an \
equivalence of ringed topoi rather than of quasi-coherent modules alone"
  AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.isFiniteType_iff_pullbackModules

add_to_stacks 05VG "of finite presentation; local properties, with the comparison of 03DX \
carried as an equivalence of ringed topoi rather than of quasi-coherent modules alone"
  AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.isFinitePresentation_iff_pullbackModules

end
